WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:29.510
People are queued up and determined to make
their voices heard.

00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:34.800
This is just one of at least 120,000 polling
stations across the huge country.

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:37.079
There is anticipation in the air.

00:00:37.079 --> 00:00:38.590
But also concern and skepticism.

00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:45.820
There is concern about violence and doubts
whether the election is going to go ahead

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:49.860
without any major disruptions.

00:00:49.860 --> 00:01:00.650
But as you can see people are lined up, some
here are camping for hours to get to the top

00:01:00.650 --> 00:01:02.770
of the line and cast their ballot.

00:01:02.770 --> 00:01:06.899
So the overwhelming feeling is excitement
about the elections.

00:01:06.899 --> 00:01:11.390
But it’s not just about who is going to
win it what’s at stake today.

00:01:11.390 --> 00:01:20.720
Whatever happens during and after the elections
will say a lot about the state of this still

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:25.590
very fragile democracy – 20 since the end
of military rule.

00:01:25.590 --> 00:01:31.399
There are more than 14 million newly registered
voters compared to 2015.

00:01:31.399 --> 00:01:33.899
Many of them are first time voters.

00:01:33.899 --> 00:01:38.390
Especially young people want change – and
are ready to vote Buhari out.

00:01:38.390 --> 00:01:40.710
"A lot of us are not happy.

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:44.729
There is bloodshed; the government is not
doing a lot about what is happening in this

00:01:44.729 --> 00:01:45.729
country.

00:01:45.729 --> 00:01:47.099
Really let’s tell ourselves the truth."

00:01:47.099 --> 00:01:51.460
Others believe, not everything was bad under
the incumbent President Buhari.

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:58.679
"He has fought corruption and actually he
has provided a direction."

00:01:58.679 --> 00:02:03.380
Before you can cast your ballot, you must
check if your serial number is on this wall

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:04.780
at your polling station.

00:02:04.780 --> 00:02:06.679
Grace does not find hers.

00:02:06.679 --> 00:02:07.679
She is angry.

00:02:07.679 --> 00:02:08.679
"I have checked, I have not seen my own…

00:02:08.679 --> 00:02:09.679
I saw NWOG..but supposed to be NWOH… but
I see NWOK…

00:02:09.679 --> 00:02:13.250
I have a voter's card but I cannot vote because
I don’t have my serial number, my picture

00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:15.959
is not here, I cannot vote."

00:02:15.959 --> 00:02:20.270
Things are a bit chaotic this morning, but
in the end an official assured Grace she can

00:02:20.270 --> 00:02:22.520
vote regardless of the register number.

00:02:22.520 --> 00:02:27.440
How this election will play out, how fair,
free and transparent it will be, will help

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:30.000
determine the future of the country.

